CASE = [
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> Rohit lives in Lucknow with his grandparents, parents, an uncle and two cousins. When his grandfather was ill, everyone shared the work: his mother cooked, his uncle took grandfather to the doctor and the cousins helped with school notes. Rohit's friend Ali lives only with his parents and a sister in another city. "
   "(i) What type of family is Rohit's? (ii) What type of family is Ali's? (iii) Name one advantage of Rohit's type of family shown here. (iv) Why do families remain important even when they become smaller?",
   "(i) A joint family (1). (ii) A nuclear family (1). (iii) Sharing of work and care of the elderly (1). (iv) The family still provides love, care and security (1) and teaches values such as sharing and cooperation to children (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> In Jhabua, Madhya Pradesh, the Bhil community follows a tradition called 'halma', where people come together to help one another in a crisis, such as building a house or fighting a drought. Under the Shivganga movement, led by Mahesh Sharma, villagers worked together on water conservation, and he was awarded the Padma Shri. "
   "(i) Which community follows the tradition of halma? (ii) What is halma? (iii) What did the Shivganga movement work to conserve? (iv) How does this case show that communities depend on cooperation?",
   "(i) The Bhils (1). (ii) A tradition of coming together to help one another (1). (iii) Water (1). (iv) Villagers pooled labour and effort for a common goal (1); no single household could solve the water problem alone, so cooperation benefited the whole community (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> During the 2015 floods in Chennai, many neighbours, volunteer groups and students cooked food, shared boats and gave shelter to people whose homes were under water. Later, residents of many colonies formed groups to clean the streets together. "
   "(i) Which city faced floods in 2015 in this case? (ii) Name one way in which people helped. (iii) Which Indian value, meaning selfless service, is shown? (iv) Explain how this shows interdependence in a community.",
   "(i) Chennai (1). (ii) Any one: cooking and distributing food, providing shelter, boats or cleaning (1). (iii) Seva (1). (iv) Those affected depended on others for help (1); the same helpers will need support in their turn, so each member depends on others (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
]

